course: dictionary
lesson: 5024
title: Ingenious: clever at inventing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ingenious means very clever at inventing things or finding new ways to solve problems. Look at the context for clues: an invention, a new answer, or a problem solved in a surprising way.
explain: «An ingenious idea» is a clever idea that nobody had thought of before. The wheel and Velcro are ingenious inventions because they solved problems in new ways.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. In the song, «Ingenious Mr. Toad» is said with a wink, because his motor-car ends up in a pond. The clues show that the word is being used as a joke.
fact: Ingenious means very clever at inventing things or finding new ways to solve problems.
fact: Ingenuity is the noun: it is the cleverness itself, as in «the ingenuity of the inventor».
fact: Ingeniously is the adverb: «She solved the puzzle ingeniously.»
fact: In the Just So Stories, Taffy and her father Tegumai are ingenious: they invent letters from pictures and sounds.
fact: A good check is to swap in clever or inventive and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The wheel was an ingenious invention that made moving heavy loads much easier.» What does ingenious mean here? | *Very clever at finding new ways to solve problems | Very old and dusty | Very noisy | Very large and heavy
exercise: «Taffy and her father made an ingenious way to write words using pictures and sounds.» Which word is the noun for the cleverness itself? | ingeniously | ingenious | *ingenuity | inventor
exercise: In the song, «Ingenious Mr. Toad» is a joke. Why? | He is a real genius who never makes mistakes | *His clever-sounding plans end with his car in a pond | Toads cannot drive cars | The song is about the weather
test: «The puzzle was solved ingeniously, with a trick nobody had tried before.» What does ingeniously mean? | Slowly and carefully | In a sad and tired way | *In a very clever, inventive way | Noisily and quickly
test: Which word means nearly the same as ingenious? | *Inventive | Clumsy | Barely | Glum
exam: Which sentence uses ingenious correctly? | The cat was ingenious at sleeping all day | The soup was ingenious and cold | *She built a clever machine that opened the gate by itself | The ingenious rain fell softly on the roof
